#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:3
msgid "気体1 molはなぜ22.4 Lなのか？"
msgstr "Why Does One Mole of Gas Occupy 22.4 L?"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:5
msgid ""
"高校の化学では「0 ℃、1気圧で、気体1 molの体積は約22.4 L」と習います。\\ 1 "
"molには約6.02×10²³個もの粒子があります。\\ 粒子が動き回る気体に、なぜ決まった体積があるのでしょうか。"
msgstr ""
"In high school chemistry, we learn that at 0 °C and 1 atm, one mole of "
"gas occupies about 22.4 L. \\ One mole contains about 6.02×10²³ "
"particles. \\ Why does a gas whose particles are constantly moving have a"
" definite volume?"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:9
msgid ""
"ここではアルゴン（Ar）原子を1,000個だけ用意し、箱の大きさを変えたときの圧力を計算します。\\ "
"その結果から、1気圧に対応するモル体積を求めてみましょう。\\ 使うのは、原子の運動を追う分子動力学（MD）という方法です。"
msgstr ""
"We use just 1,000 argon (Ar) atoms to calculate the pressure at different"
" box sizes. \\ Let’s use those results to find the molar volume at 1 atm."
" \\ The method is molecular dynamics (MD), which tracks the motion of the"
" atoms."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:14
msgid "計算対象と計算条件"
msgstr "Systems and Calculation Conditions"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:16
msgid ""
"Arは原子が一つずつ独立に動く単原子気体です。\\ 原子間の力には、Quloudに登録されたArモデル（ ``argon_vrabec`` "
"）を使います。\\ 近づきすぎると反発し、少し離れたところで弱く引き合う、Lennard-Jones（LJ）型のモデルです。\\ 計算条件を "
":numref:`tab-argon-conditions` にまとめます。\\ 立方体のセルの一辺を27〜40 "
"nmの6通りに変え、それぞれの圧力を求めます。\\ このうち一辺33.3879144 nmは、理想気体ならちょうど1 atm（1.01325 "
"bar）になる体積です。\\ 各体積では、乱数のシード（乱数列を生成するための初期値）を変えた3つの計算を行い、結果を平均します。\\ "
"シードを変えると、原子の初期配置と初期速度、温度制御に使う乱数が変わります。\\ 力場の数値パラメータ、入力構造、解析の手順は "
":doc:`reproduction` で確認できます。"
msgstr ""
"Ar is a monatomic gas whose atoms move individually. \\ For the forces "
"between atoms, we use the Ar model registered in Quloud "
"(``argon_vrabec``). \\ It is a Lennard-Jones (LJ) type model: atoms repel"
" one another when they come too close and attract one another weakly at "
"somewhat larger distances. \\ The calculation conditions are summarized "
"in :numref:`tab-argon-conditions`. \\ We vary the side length of the "
"cubic cell over six values from 27 to 40 nm and determine the pressure "
"for each. \\ Of these, the cell with a side length of 33.3879144 nm has "
"the volume at which an ideal gas would be at exactly 1 atm (1.01325 bar)."
" \\ For each volume, we run three calculations with different random "
"seeds (the initial values used to generate sequences of random numbers) "
"and average the results. \\ Changing the seed changes the initial "
"positions and velocities of the atoms and the random numbers used for "
"temperature control. \\ The numerical force field parameters, input "
"structures, and analysis steps are available in :doc:`reproduction`."

