#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:49
msgid ""
"一辺33.3879144 nmのセルの計算結果を :numref:`fig-argon-snapshot` に示します。\\ "
"セルには壁がありません。ある面から出た原子は反対側に現れます。\\ この周期境界条件によって、広く続く気体の一部分を表しています。\\ "
"図ではセル中央の厚さ2 nmの部分を取り出し、見やすいように原子を大きく描いています。\\ "
"1原子あたりの体積の立方根、つまり原子の平均的な間隔は約3.34 nmで、相互作用の長さの目安であるσ＝0.33952 nmの約10倍です。\\ "
"原子どうしの間隔が、相互作用を打ち切る距離（1.2 nm）よりも広い、希薄な気体です。"
msgstr ""
":numref:`fig-argon-snapshot` shows the results for the cell with a side "
"length of 33.3879144 nm. \\ The cell has no walls. An atom that leaves "
"through one face reappears on the opposite side. \\ With these periodic "
"boundary conditions, the cell represents a small portion of an extended "
"gas. \\ The figure shows a 2 nm thick slice through the center of the "
"cell, with the atoms enlarged for visibility. \\ The cube root of the "
"volume per atom, that is, the average spacing between atoms, is about "
"3.34 nm, roughly 10 times the characteristic interaction length σ = "
"0.33952 nm. \\ This is a dilute gas in which the atoms are farther apart "
"than the distance at which the interactions are cut off (1.2 nm)."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:61
msgid ""
"Ar 1,000原子の440 ps時点の座標から、セル中央の厚さ2 nmに含まれる原子だけをxy平面へ投影した図です。\\ "
"軸の単位はnm、セルの一辺は約33.388 nmです。\\ 円の表示半径0.50 nmは、LJのσ/2＝0.16976 "
"nmの約2.95倍です。\\ 黒線は図に含まれる5原子の430〜440 "
"psの保存座標を結んだ経路です。経路は厚さ方向に部分領域の外へ出ることもあります。\\ 周期境界をまたぐ線分は描いていません。\\ "
"四角はセルの境界を示し、壁を表すものではありません。"
msgstr ""
"The figure projects the saved coordinates at 440 ps onto the xy plane, "
"showing only the Ar atoms within the central 2 nm slice of the 1,000-atom"
" cell. \\ The axes are in nm and the cell is about 33.388 nm on a side. "
"\\ The circles have a display radius of 0.50 nm, about 2.95 times the LJ "
"value σ/2 = 0.16976 nm. \\ The black lines connect the saved coordinates "
"from 430 to 440 ps for the five atoms shown. The paths can extend out of "
"the slice in the thickness direction. \\ Line segments that cross a "
"periodic boundary are omitted. \\ The square marks the cell boundary and "
"represents no physical wall."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:69
msgid "理想気体の予想"
msgstr "Ideal Gas Predictions"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:71
msgid "計算結果と比べるため、まず理想気体の式を確認します。"
msgstr ""
"We first review the ideal gas equations for comparison with the "
"calculation results."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:73
msgid "PV=nRT"
msgstr "PV=nRT"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:78
msgid ":math:`n` が物質量（モル）です。両辺をこれで割ると、"
msgstr ""
"In this equation, :math:`n` is the amount of substance in moles. Dividing"
" both sides by it gives"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:80
msgid "PV_m=RT"
msgstr "PV_m=RT"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:85
msgid ""
"ここで :math:`P` は圧力、:math:`T` は絶対温度、:math:`R` は気体定数です。\\ モル体積 :math:`V_m` "
"は、体積を物質量で割った「1 molあたりの体積」です。\\ 温度を一定値、例えば 0 ℃（= 273.15 "
"K）にそろえれば、右辺は定数なので、圧力はモル体積に反比例し、体積が小さくなれば圧力は高くなるはずです。\\ "
"以下では、MDで求めた圧力がこの関係からどれだけずれるかを調べます。"
msgstr ""
"Here, :math:`P` is pressure, :math:`T` is absolute temperature, and "
":math:`R` is the gas constant. \\ The molar volume :math:`V_m` is the "
"volume divided by the amount of substance, or the volume per mole. \\ At "
"a fixed temperature, such as 0 °C (= 273.15 K), the right-hand side is "
"constant, so pressure is inversely proportional to molar volume and "
"should rise as the volume decreases. \\ Below, we examine how far the MD "
"pressures deviate from this relationship."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:91
msgid "圧力の時間変化"
msgstr "Pressure over Time"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:93
msgid ""
"MDの圧力は、どの時刻でも同じ値になるわけではありません。\\ 一辺33.3879144 nm、シード1101の計算の圧力と温度の変化を "
":numref:`fig-argon-pressure-time` に示します。\\ "
"この希薄な条件では、圧力の揺らぎの主な原因は温度、つまり運動エネルギーの揺らぎです。\\ 測定温度の標準偏差は約7 "
"K（約2.6%）で、瞬間圧力の相対的な幅と同程度です。\\ そこで、揺らぎをならすために圧力を時間平均します。\\ 最初の40 "
"psは平均から除き、残りの400 psを測定区間とします。"
msgstr ""
"MD pressure does not take the same value at every moment. \\ The pressure"
" and temperature over time for the calculation with a side length of "
"33.3879144 nm and seed 1101 are shown in :numref:`fig-argon-pressure-"
"time`. \\ At this low density, pressure fluctuations mainly come from "
"fluctuations in temperature, and thus in kinetic energy. \\ The measured "
"temperature has a standard deviation of about 7 K (approximately 2.6%), "
"comparable to the relative spread of the instantaneous pressure. \\ We "
"therefore average the pressure over time to smooth out the fluctuations. "
"\\ We exclude the first 40 ps from the average and use the remaining 400 "
"ps as the production period."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:105
msgid ""
"一辺33.3879144 nm、シード1101の計算です。\\ 上段はEDRから0.1 ps間隔で抽出した圧力（薄線）と10 "
"psの移動平均（青線）、\\ 下段は温度です。横軸は時間（ps）、縦軸はそれぞれbar、Kです。\\ 黄色の0〜40 "
"psは平均から除いた区間です。\\ 破線は、上段が理想気体の式による圧力（1.01325 bar）、下段が設定温度の273.15 Kです。"
msgstr ""
"The cell is 33.3879144 nm on a side and the seed is 1101. \\ The top "
"panel shows pressure sampled from the EDR every 0.1 ps (light line) and "
"its 10 ps moving average (blue line), \\ and the bottom panel shows "
"temperature. The horizontal axis shows time (ps), and the vertical axes "
"use bar and K, respectively. \\ The yellow region from 0 to 40 ps is "
"excluded from the average. \\ The dashed lines mark the pressure from the"
" ideal gas equation (1.01325 bar) in the top panel and the set "
"temperature of 273.15 K in the bottom panel."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:111
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"このシードでは、測定区間の平均圧力は1.01192 bar、ブロック平均による標準誤差は約0.00066 barでした。\\ "
"隣り合う時刻の圧力は互いに相関しているので、測定区間を同じ長さのブロックに分けてブロックごとに平均し、そのばらつきから標準誤差を求めます。\\ "
"ブロックの長さを5〜80 psに変えて標準誤差を調べ、最大の値を採用しています（ :numref:`{number}. {name} <gas-"
"reproduction-statistics>` ）。\\ "
"これは今回の区間で見積もった統計精度であり、あらゆる系統誤差がなくなったことを意味しません。"
msgstr ""
"For this seed, the mean pressure over the production period was 1.01192 "
"bar, with a standard error of about 0.00066 bar from block averaging. \\ "
"Because pressures at neighboring times are correlated with one another, "
"we divide the production period into blocks of equal length, average each"
" block, and obtain the standard error from the spread of the block "
"averages. \\ We examined the standard error for block lengths from 5 to "
"80 ps and adopted the largest value (:numref:`{number}. {name} <gas-"
"reproduction-statistics>`). \\ This is the statistical precision "
"estimated for this interval and does not mean that all systematic errors "
"have been eliminated."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:117
