#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:166
msgid ""
"理想気体の列は :eq:`eq-gas-ideal` による値です。\\ "
"MD平均の列は、シードごとに測定区間の時間平均を求め、3つのシードで平均した値です。\\ "
"標準誤差は、時間相関を考慮したブロック平均とシード間のばらつきから求めています。\\ "
"この誤差には、原子間相互作用のモデルや粒子数の有限性による偏りは含めていません。\\ "
"どの体積でも、MDの圧力は理想気体の値より0.11〜0.22%低く、体積が小さいほど差が大きい傾向があります。"
msgstr ""
"The ideal gas column gives values from Equation :eq:`eq-gas-ideal`. \\ "
"For the MD mean column, we computed the time average over the production "
"period for each seed and then averaged over the three seeds. \\ The "
"standard error is obtained from block averaging, which accounts for time "
"correlations, and from the variation across seeds. \\ This error does not"
" include biases due to the model for interatomic interactions or the "
"finite number of particles. \\ At every volume, the MD pressure was "
"0.11–0.22% below the ideal gas value, and the difference tends to be "
"larger at smaller volumes."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:173
msgid "1気圧に対応するモル体積"
msgstr "Molar Volume at 1 atm"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:175
msgid ""
":numref:`fig-argon-pv` の上段に各体積の圧力を、下段に理想気体からのずれを示します。\\ "
"上段では、体積を小さくすると圧力が上がり、全体として理想気体の曲線に近い関係になっています。\\ この上段の測定値から1 "
"atmのモル体積を求め、下段で理想気体との差の原因を調べます。"
msgstr ""
"The top panel of :numref:`fig-argon-pv` shows the pressure at each "
"volume, and the bottom panel shows the deviation from the ideal gas. \\ "
"In the top panel, pressure rises as the volume decreases, and the overall"
" relationship is close to the ideal gas curve. \\ We obtain the molar "
"volume at 1 atm from the measurements in the top panel and examine the "
"cause of the difference from the ideal gas in the bottom panel."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:184
msgid ""
"上段の横軸はモル体積（L/mol）、縦軸は圧力（bar）です。\\ 点と誤差棒は :numref:`tab-argon-pv` "
"と同じMD平均と1標準誤差で、誤差棒は点より小さい場合があります。\\ 黒線は式 :eq:`eq-gas-ideal` の予測、水平破線は1 "
"atm＝1.01325 bar、点線は一辺30、33、33.3879144、36 nmの測定値に対する近傍フィットです。\\ "
"下段の横軸は逆モル体積1/Vm（mol/L）、縦軸は圧縮因子Z＝PVm/(RT)で、理想気体ではZ＝1です。\\ "
"黒線は理想気体、灰破線は全体の重心運動の除去だけを考えた予測、緑点線はさらに打ち切りLJの二体相互作用を加えた273.15 Kの予測です。\\ "
"橙の×印は、緑点線の予測を各体積の実測平均温度へ補正した値です。いずれの予測も、パラメータをMD圧力に合わせて決めてはいません。"
msgstr ""
"In the top panel, the horizontal axis shows molar volume (L/mol) and the "
"vertical axis shows pressure (bar). \\ The points and error bars show the"
" same MD means and one standard error as in :numref:`tab-argon-pv`; the "
"error bars can be smaller than the markers. \\ The black curve is the "
"prediction from Equation :eq:`eq-gas-ideal`, the horizontal dashed line "
"marks 1 atm = 1.01325 bar, and the dotted curve is the local fit to the "
"measurements for side lengths of 30, 33, 33.3879144, and 36 nm. \\ In the"
" bottom panel, the horizontal axis shows the inverse molar volume 1/Vm "
"(mol/L) and the vertical axis shows the compressibility factor Z = "
"PVm/(RT), which equals 1 for an ideal gas. \\ The black line is the ideal"
" gas, the gray dashed line is the prediction that accounts only for "
"removal of the motion of the system’s center of mass, and the green "
"dotted curve is the prediction at 273.15 K that also includes truncated "
"LJ pair interactions. \\ The orange crosses mark the predictions of the "
"green dotted curve corrected to the measured mean temperature at each "
"volume. None of the predictions has parameters fitted to the MD "
"pressures."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:191
msgid ""
"1 atmは1 barと少し違い、1.01325 barです。\\ この圧力付近の4体積の測定値に :math:`P=a/V_m+b` "
"を当てはめ、係数を自由に決めました。\\ 22.4 Lという値はフィットに使っていません。\\ 得られた1 atmのモル体積は **22.383 "
"± 0.012 L/mol** です。\\ ±は統計的なフィットの1標準誤差です。\\ 推定法と共分散は配布データの "
"``pv_fit.json`` に保存しています。"
msgstr ""
"One atmosphere differs slightly from 1 bar and equals 1.01325 bar. \\ We "
"fitted :math:`P=a/V_m+b` to the measurements at four volumes near this "
"pressure, with both coefficients free. \\ The fit did not use the value "
"22.4 L. \\ The resulting molar volume at 1 atm is **22.383 ± 0.012 "
"L/mol**. \\ The uncertainty after ± is one statistical standard error of "
"the fit. \\ The estimation method and covariance are in ``pv_fit.json`` "
"in the downloadable data."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:198
msgid "一方、理想気体の予測は次の値です。"
msgstr "The ideal gas prediction, by comparison, is"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:200
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"V_m&=\\frac{RT}{P}=22.413969545\\ \\mathrm{L/mol},\\\\\n"
"T&=273.15\\ \\mathrm{K},\\quad P=101325\\ \\mathrm{Pa}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"V_m&=\\frac{RT}{P}=22.413969545\\ \\mathrm{L/mol},\\\\\n"
"T&=273.15\\ \\mathrm{K},\\quad P=101325\\ \\mathrm{Pa}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:207
msgid ""
"MDの推定は理想値より約0.14%小さく、どちらも有効数字3桁では約22.4 L/molになります。\\ "
"この差の原因を、圧力の中身から考えます。\\ GROMACSは、原子の運動エネルギーによる部分と原子間力による部分から圧力を計算します [1]_ "
"。\\ 温度を一定に保つと運動エネルギーの平均が決まるので、運動による部分は理想気体の式と同じ形になります。\\ "
"理想気体からのずれは、主に次の二つの効果で説明できます。\\ "
"一つは運動による部分の補正です。計算では全体の重心の運動を取り除いているので、運動の自由度が3つ減り、原子1,000個では圧力が約0.10%小さくなります。\\"
" もう一つは原子間力による部分で、今回の打ち切りLJモデルの引力は、理想気体に近い密度での独立な見積もりでは、1 "
"atm付近で約0.07%、今回の体積の範囲では約0.04〜0.13%だけ圧力を下げます。\\ 平均温度が指定値より約0.07 "
"K高かった効果（約+0.02%）も合わせると、1 atm付近では約−0.15%の予測になります。\\ :numref:`fig-argon-pv`"
" の下段のとおり、6体積の各測定値とこの予測との差は、いずれも統計標準誤差の0.5倍以内でした。\\ 見積もりの式と数値積分は "
":doc:`reproduction` にまとめています。\\ "
"この一致は今回の有限個の粒子と相互作用モデルについての確認であり、実在Arの状態方程式を高精度に決めたという意味ではありません。"
msgstr ""
"The MD estimate is about 0.14% below the ideal value, and both are about "
"22.4 L/mol to three significant figures. \\ To find the cause of this "
"difference, we look at what makes up the pressure. \\ GROMACS calculates "
"pressure from a part due to the kinetic energy of the atoms and a part "
"due to interatomic forces [1]_. \\ At constant temperature, the mean "
"kinetic energy is fixed, so the kinetic part has the same form as the "
"ideal gas equation. \\ The deviation from the ideal gas can be explained "
"mainly by the following two effects. \\ The first is a correction to the "
"kinetic part. Because the calculation removes the motion of the system’s "
"center of mass, the number of degrees of freedom of motion decreases by "
"three, and for 1,000 atoms the pressure is about 0.10% lower. \\ The "
"second is the part due to interatomic forces. According to an independent"
" estimate at densities close to those of an ideal gas, the attraction in "
"the truncated LJ model used here lowers the pressure by about 0.07% near "
"1 atm and by about 0.04–0.13% over the range of volumes studied. \\ "
"Including the effect of the mean temperature being about 0.07 K above the"
" specified value (about +0.02%), the predicted deviation near 1 atm is "
"about −0.15%. \\ :numref:`fig-argon-pv` shows in its bottom panel that, "
"at all six volumes, the difference between each measurement and this "
"prediction was within 0.5 statistical standard errors. \\ The equations "
"and numerical integration for the estimate are described in "
":doc:`reproduction`. \\ This agreement is a check only for the finite "
"number of particles and the interaction model used here. It does not mean"
" that the equation of state of real Ar has been determined with high "
"precision."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:220
msgid "この数値実験から分かること"
msgstr "What the Numerical Experiment Shows"

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:222
msgid ""
"原子1,000個のMDから求めた0 ℃・1 atmのモル体積は22.383 ± 0.012 L/molで、理想気体の22.414 "
"L/molより約0.14%小さい値でした。\\ この差は、全体の重心運動の除去と、モデルの原子間の引力による圧力の低下で説明できました。"
msgstr ""
"The molar volume at 0 °C and 1 atm obtained from MD with 1,000 atoms was "
"22.383 ± 0.012 L/mol, about 0.14% smaller than the ideal gas value of "
"22.414 L/mol. \\ This difference could be explained by the removal of the"
" motion of the system’s center of mass and the reduction in pressure due "
"to the attraction between atoms in the model."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:225
msgid ""
"22.4 Lは、原子1個が占める決まった大きさではありません。\\ 温度と圧力を指定したときに、多数の粒子の運動から現れる体積です。\\ "
"この数値実験では、その値に近い体積を、有限個のArの運動と圧力から求められました。\\ "
"理想気体の式をゼロから証明する計算でも、実在気体の高精度な状態方程式を決める計算でもありません。"
msgstr ""
"The value 22.4 L is not a fixed size that a single atom occupies. \\ It "
"is a volume that emerges from the motion of many particles at a specified"
" temperature and pressure. \\ In this numerical experiment, we obtained a"
" volume close to that value from the motion and pressure of a finite "
"number of Ar atoms. \\ The calculation neither proves the ideal gas "
"equation from scratch nor establishes a high-precision equation of state "
"for a real gas."

#: ../../gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.rst:230
msgid "次の :doc:`five_gases_avogadro` では、分子の質量を変えたときの速さと圧力を比較します。"
msgstr ""
"In the next part, :doc:`five_gases_avogadro`, we compare speeds and "
"pressures as the molecular mass changes."

